  message: "P2 REVIEW 2026-11-01 (dev 24d0b860ee; owner-requested re-check of the 51 open P2 violated/todo_hard/todo_soft items; fixtures and outputs under ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/p2_review_11012026/C1/). VERDICT: CURRENT by code read (no cold embedding run; the 433 count not re-measured). sketch.py:4604 _select_additional_files; candidates = every non-source, non-excluded file (:4677-4687); :4708-4713 batch_embed_files(candidate_files, ...) embeds ALL of them when _has_sentence_transformers(); semantic_top_n=10 (call :7132) and the budget-derived max_files (:7103) apply afterwards; survey's cached_centrality_scores (cli.py:13548) is used for ranking only (:4733-4738), never to pre-filter. Embeddings are content-hash cached, so only a cold run pays; INV-gujus (9679de97c5) changed fetch policy only, and this box has the weights. MECHANISM: rank-then-truncate - the expensive per-candidate score is computed over the full set before any cheap pre-filter or the display budget (singleton). Status unchanged."  # 440b
- op: discuss  # e664
  at: '2026-11-13T11:08:49Z'  # e664
  by: agent  # e664
  actor: jgstern_agent  # e664
  clock: 3  # e664
  nonce: e664  # e664
  message: "MEASURED 2026-11-13, then PLAN (owner asked for the fix; owner steer during the work: \"try TF-IDF or BM25; not sure embeddings help\", then \"or much larger samplings of the seed passages\" from the local well-known-repo clones). Instrument: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/patof_embedding_prefilter_11132026/. (1) COST, cold, 6 cores: about 0.16-0.31 s per candidate whatever its length; 25 s for 153 files (killbill), 115 s for 451 (this repo), 239 s for 958 (kserve), 423 s for 1,379 (keycloak, under load). (2) THE ITEM'S OWN QUESTION, a top-K pre-filter: no cheap order reproduces the embedding's top 4 (0.5-1.0 recall from a 64-file shortlist), and the embedding does not reproduce ITSELF: re-seeding its sampling keeps 3 of its top 4 on three repos and 0-1 of 4 on this one (265 of 451 scores move; two byte-identical READMEs scored 0.717 and 0.678, ranks 1 and 21). (3) DOES IT FIND USEFUL FILES: label = candidates the repo's own README links to. On the six repos where the embedding ran, it put 4 of 37 linked files in the top ten; documentation-role-then-depth put 13. On 444 well-known repos (no embedding; split by repo, test scored once after the design was frozen): role, depth, then BM25 against the three probe paragraphs R@10 0.72 on 46 test repos (233 labels); BM25 alone 0.53; BM25 with 630 seed passages from 258 train repos 0.55; shuffled 0.24. The larger seed sampling did not help: location and role carry the signal, wording is a tie-break. PLAN: remove the embedding from Additional Files; replace the list it fed with overview_rank.rank_overview_files (role, depth, BM25 on the probes, path). No model load, no cache, deterministic, identical with or without sentence-transformers. Record as docs/measurements/0033. RESIDUAL to file after the merge: the ModernBERT path (batch_embed_files and friends, the second model install-embeddings fetches) will have no caller."  # e664
