- op: discuss  # 38e3
  at: '2026-11-13T13:47:23Z'  # 38e3
  by: agent  # 38e3
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 38e3
  clock: 5  # 38e3
  nonce: '38e3'  # 38e3
  message: "Fixed in PR #2170 (dev ad78277020; commits \"Additional Files is ranked without an embedding model\" and \"remove the embedding path Additional Files no longer uses\"). The Additional Files list that came from an embedding ranking is now overview_rank.rank_overview_files: documentation before configuration, shallower first, BM25 of the first 4,000 characters against six probe paragraphs as the tie-break, then path. (CORRECTION to my plan note above: the probe list holds SIX paragraphs, who/what/when/where/why/how, not three; the scripts used the whole list, so the numbers stand.) EVIDENCE, behaviour: the ranking of this repo's 451 candidates takes 0.07 s (kserve 958: 0.09 s; keycloak 1,379: 0.15 s) where the cold embedding took 115 s, 239 s and 423 s; a sketch on a cached survey ran end to end in 33.7 s at 8k and 32.9 s at 32k with no \"Embedding additional files\" phase (hypergumbo sketch . -t 8000 / -t 32000 on dev+branch, 2026-11-13). No model is loaded: tests patch every loader to raise and the selection is unchanged with sentence-transformers present, absent or broken. Why this ranking and not a pre-filter in front of the embedding: docs/measurements/0033 (the embedding did not reproduce itself, and put 4 of 37 README-linked files in the top ten where role and depth put 13; on 46 held-out repositories the shipped order has R@10 0.72 against 0.53 for content similarity alone). The owner's two suggestions were both run: BM25/TF-IDF (content similarity does not beat location) and a larger seed sampling (630 linked documents from 258 repositories as the BM25 query: 0.55, same as the probes). NOT ASSERTED: that the new order is the best ranking of documentation; README links are a stand-in label (0033, \"What this does not support\"). A full cold self-run was not re-timed end to end after the change."  # 38e3
